# Whether an interval of the round-up interval is the whole line, (+inf, +inf); the default
# interval_entire_1 on the meaning. Exact, in every rounding mode (docs/developer/design/upward.md,
# "Predicates and comparisons"). Requires the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and
# the options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_entire_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
ensures:       certain m entire x x=xu,xn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        both lanes compared with +inf (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand

a = eq(xu, const inf)
b = eq(xn, const inf)
m = and(a, b)
